{%- comment -%}
  Kept deliberately, and not yet called from anywhere.

  The cart page now writes its own form, but this stays for a second cart surface.

  Theme Check reports this as `OrphanedSnippet`, and that report is correct:
  nothing calls it yet. It is a warning, not an error, and it stands until the
  file is wired up - which is the fix, rather than silencing the check.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% doc %}
  Wraps the cart page.

  Everything inside is a real `<form action="/cart" method="post">`. Quantity
  inputs are named `updates[]` and the checkout button is a real submit, so with
  JavaScript disabled the page still updates quantities and reaches checkout.

  @param {string} children - Captured cart blocks
  @param {string} section_id

  @example
    {% render 'cart-items-component', children: cart_items_children, section_id: section.id %}
{% enddoc %}

<form action="{{ routes.cart_url }}" method="post" class="cart-page__form" data-section-id="{{ section_id }}">
  {{ children }}
</form>
